---
description: RQS mastering engine safety workflow
alwaysApply: true
---

Work only on the current feature branch.

Before modifying DSP:
1. Read the current implementation and all callers.
2. Separate confirmed facts from hypotheses.
3. Add a test reproducing the problem before implementing a fix.
4. Never overwrite source audio.
5. Never call a limiter True Peak unless final dBTP is independently measured.
6. Never use sys.exit() inside DSP library code.
7. Do not modify creative DSP and infrastructure in the same task.
8. Preserve public API unless explicitly approved.
9. Run pytest after every implementation step.
10. Show git diff and exact test results before committing.
11. Do not add dependencies without license and compatibility analysis.
12. Never commit credentials, environment files or test audio.
13. Do not silently change sample rate, channel layout or output format.
14. Validate final WAV after writing and reopening it.
